cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "behavioral-fsm-benchmark: Behavioral Evaluation of LLM-Generated FSMs"
message: "If you use this benchmark or framework, please cite using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sanchez
    given-names: Cesar Andres
repository-code: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/behavioral-fsm-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/behavioral-fsm-benchmark"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-03
keywords:
  - finite state machines
  - large language models
  - behavioral correctness
  - model-based testing
  - robustness
  - reproducibility
  - empirical software engineering
abstract: >
  behavioral-fsm-benchmark extends FSM-Bench-20 (IST 2026) with behavioral
  oracles, gold reference FSMs, guard-aware determinism, test-suite agreement,
  equivalence checking, robustness perturbations, and multi-run reproducibility
  instrumentation for EMSE submission.
